// EXPECT_COMPILE_ERROR accepts 1 or 2 arguments, but 0 were given
//
// [M-196-freefn-arity-overload-default-ret-mismatch] NEGATIVE guard: the
// `pick_no_default_overload` fix (types/mod.rs) must NOT swallow a genuine
// wrong-arity call — calling with FEWER args than either overload's
// REQUIRED (non-default) param count binds against NEITHER candidate
// (`bind_call_args` fails for both — `MissingRequired` on the shared
// required `x`), so `overload_applicability` returns `None` for both and
// the fix's tie-break is never reached.
//
// THE GAP THIS FIXTURE DOCUMENTED IS CLOSED (registry #921, 2026-09-04), and
// the expectation is TIGHTENED rather than merely repaired. Its previous
// header described the state of the world exactly: the checker's own
// `any_arity` stayed `false`, the code deferred the arity error to BoundCtx —
// "reported by BoundCtx, not here" — "but BoundCtx does not fire here
// either", so the call leaked all the way to a codegen "no matching overload"
// and the fixture pinned it loosely, "regardless of exact diagnostic owner".
//
// That was an honest description of a hole, written by the window that hit it,
// and it went unfixed for two months because a fixture pinning the leak stayed
// green while the leak persisted. The checker now refuses the call itself, at
// the call site, naming both the declared arities and the count supplied. So
// the pattern moves from the loose codegen phrasing to the precise checker
// one: the same program is still refused, by a better tool, with a message a
// reader can act on. Loosening it back would restore the very silence #921 is
// about.
module neg.m196af_freefn_arity_default_ret_neg

// D246-амендмент ([M-ro-launder-via-mut-binding], Ф.2 миграция, 2026-07-23):
// `tag` — `mut` (was bare) — passthrough return of a bare `ro`-param under
// mut-default return type triggers the (unrelated-to-this-test's-purpose)
// new return-position check; `mut` sidesteps it without touching what this
// file actually probes (arity-overload ambiguity). Harmless for `str`
// (buffer always immutable by construction — see D26).
fn m196af_np(x int) -> int => x
fn m196af_np(x int, mut tag str = "d") -> str => tag

test "unreachable — codegen must fail before running" {
    assert(m196af_np() == 0)
}
